      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "As-cast equiatomic HfMoTaTiZr has a density of approximately 10.21 g/cm³.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "As-cast HfMoTaTiZr has high strength at room and elevated temperatures.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A portion of Hf should be replaced by additional Zr.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Partial replacement of Hf by Zr will reduce the alloy density.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9506522::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf is heavier than Zr.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf and Zr have comparable atomic sizes.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hf-to-Zr substitution will retain a single-phase solid solution, likely BCC.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9506522::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will retain lattice distortion similar to that of the initial alloy.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Retained lattice distortion will largely preserve solid-solution strengthening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9506522::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Zr has been shown to maintain elevated-temperature strength in similar alloy systems.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy's room-temperature yield strength and ductility will remain comparable to those of as-cast HfMoTaTiZr.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9506522::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy's yield strength and ductility at approximately 1000 °C will remain comparable to those of as-cast HfMoTaTiZr.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed benefit applies from room temperature to approximately 1000 °C under standard tensile or compression loading.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The amount of density reduction and mechanical-property retention will depend on the Hf substitution level.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A casting study should compare 10%, 20%, and 30% Hf substitution levels with the original as-cast alloy using density, mechanical, and XRD measurements.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A yield-strength or ductility decrease greater than about 10–15%, absence of a significant density reduction, or observed phase segregation would falsify the hypothesis.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.falsification_rule",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
